            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 565)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Drag to reorder the playlist.</b> Grab a clip's thumbnail in the Playlist panel and drop it where it goes — a line shows where it will land, and a version stack moves as one. The chevrons still work. Everyone in the room follows: native seats and the web review take the new order live, and someone who joins later gets it too.</li>
<li><b>The web review's playlist has thumbnails now, and they're the handles.</b> A reviewer in a browser can drag clips into a new order as well; it comes back to the app and to everyone else. Needs this build on the host.</li>
<li><b>Fixed on the web: marks, stills and the gamma menu while a grade is applied live.</b> The picture that carried your live grade sat on top of everything in the browser — reviewers couldn't see marks or the full-resolution still, and the gamma menu appeared to do nothing. All three show now, and the picture keeps its shape in any window.</li>
<li>A guest's chevrons and sorts reorder the room too, the same as a drag.</li>
<li>Under the hood, the web share's clip list follows the playlist on every update, and re-baking a clip with its grade finds that clip by name — so reordering during a long re-bake can't cross the wires.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
